# Intent: The control sheet and the bot's own settings screen. Mute, Quiet, Light, Timers, Games and the last tile are drawn icons (a speaker, a moon, a bulb, a clock, a game pad, a gear), six 44 by 44 tiles in one row, so the sheet is shorter. The top row of the sheet is the stock-style status row: Wi-Fi signal bars at the left, the time in the middle, the battery bar and percent at the right, colored by state (green good, amber low, red critical, dimmed at night). The gear tile opens a settings screen on the bot: a face style picker (Big eyes, Eyes only, Stock, Classic, Minimal, and Pictures while a picture pack is held) with a live preview of the choice, a Status icons switch, a Wi-Fi button (quick settings), a Done target 108 by 44 and the grabber handle; a swipe down closes it. A style is drawn at once and saved from the main task through maipai_face_set_style (the same flash key the settings page face style uses; the host is told by a face_style_changed event and the page reads it back with self.face.get_config), the switch through maipai_pref_set from the main task. The Games tile is a drawn die showing five (the game pad was not liked). The Wi-Fi button opens the Wi-Fi page and a new More button opens the More screens; opening the settings screen first closes any other overlay screen (patch UI09), and a page, the sheet or the face shown from a tool closes it.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_pages_core.h, maipai_pages.cc, maipai_pages.h, maipai_pages_unit.cc (ours, P10 to P13, UI01)
# Check after a flash: Swipe up for the sheet: six icon tiles, the status row on top; the gear opens Settings: tap a style and the face changes and the preview follows; the Status icons switch; swipe down closes.

